{
  "sn24.6:0.1": "Linked Discourses 24.6 ",
  "sn24.6:0.2": "1. Stream-Entry ",
  "sn24.6:0.3": "Acting ",
  "sn24.6:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn24.6:1.2": "“Mendicants, when what exists, because of grasping what and insisting on what, does the view arise: ",
  "sn24.6:1.3": "‘The one who acts does nothing wrong when they punish, mutilate, torture, aggrieve, oppress, intimidate, or when they encourage others to do the same. Nothing bad is done when they kill, steal, break into houses, plunder wealth, steal from isolated buildings, commit highway robbery, commit adultery, and lie. ",
  "sn24.6:1.4": "If you were to reduce all the living creatures of this earth to one heap and mass of flesh with a razor-edged chakram, no evil comes of that, and no outcome of evil. ",
  "sn24.6:1.5": "If you were to go along the south bank of the Ganges killing, mutilating, and torturing, and encouraging others to do the same, no evil comes of that, and no outcome of evil. ",
  "sn24.6:1.6": "If you were to go along the north bank of the Ganges giving and sacrificing and encouraging others to do the same, no merit comes of that, and no outcome of merit. ",
  "sn24.6:1.7": "In giving, self-control, restraint, and truthfulness there is no merit or outcome of merit’?” ",
  "sn24.6:1.8": "“Our teachings are rooted in the Buddha. …” ",
  "sn24.6:2.1": "“When form exists, because of grasping form and insisting on form, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.6:2.2": "‘The one who acts does nothing wrong … ",
  "sn24.6:2.3": "